Parity selection reproduced exactly from the web `useMemo` (cross-platform order/identity parity, not a
"corrected" variant):
  all = achievements ?? [] ; all.filter(a => a.unlocked && a.unlocked_at)
       .sort((a,b) => Date.parse(b.unlocked_at) - Date.parse(a.unlocked_at)).slice(0, isWide?5:3)
JS's stable Array.sort on equal timestamps is matched by an original-index tiebreak. The `!prefs.showOnDashboard`
opt-out precedes the shell loading/error states (renders the disabled empty state so the grid slot never vanishes).

i18n keys from source (parity): widget.recentlyUnlocked.title ("Recently Unlocked"),
widget.recentlyUnlocked.disabled ("Recently unlocked achievements are hidden in your settings."),
achievements.viewNamed ("View achievement: %@"), achievements.noneYet, lifetime.unlocked ("✓ Unlocked"),
widget.recentlyUnlocked (+ .description) for the registry name/description. No English literals in the view.

